      "target": "../sections/page-001.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SEVENTY-FIRST WORLD HEALTH ASSEMBLY \nWHA71.7 \nAgenda item 12.4 \n26 May 2018 \nDigital health \nThe Seventy-first World Health Assembly, \nHaving considered the report on mHealth;1 \nRecalling resolutions WHA58.28 (2005) on eHealth and WHA66.24 (2013) on eHealth \nstandardization and interoperability; \nRecognizing the potential of digital technologies to advance the Sustainable Development \nGoals, and in particular to support health systems in all countries in health promotion and disease \nprevention, and by improving the accessibility, quality and affordability of health services; \nRecognizing also",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The first page of World Health Assembly resolution WHA71.7 on digital health (26 May 2018), which recalls earlier eHealth resolutions and recognizes the potential of digital technologies to support health systems and the Sustainable Development Goals. Its preamble stresses that digital solutions should complement existing services, that human interaction remains vital, and that technology transfer and cooperation matter.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-279505/blocks/prose-page-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 2",
      "pageStart": 2,
      "pageEnd": 2,
      "target": "../sections/page-002.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHA71.7 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2 \n1. \nURGES Member States:1 \n(1) \nto assess their use of digital technologies for health, including in health information \nsystems at the national and subnational levels, in order to identify areas of improvement, and to \nprioritize, as appropriate, the development, evaluation, implementation, scale-up and greater \nutilization of digital technologies, as a means of promoting equitable, affordable and universal \naccess to health for all, including the special needs of groups that are vulnerable in the context \nof digital health;  \n(2) \nto consider, as appropriate, how digi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out what the resolution urges Member States to do, such as assess their use of digital technologies, integrate them into health systems and regulation, and build workforce digital skills. It also calls for public trust in digital health through work with civil society.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-279505/blocks/prose-page-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Page 3",
      "pageStart": 3,
      "pageEnd": 3,
      "target": "../sections/page-003.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHA71.7 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n3 \n(10) to develop, as appropriate, legislation and/or data protection policies around issues such \nas data access, sharing, consent, security, privacy, interoperability and inclusivity consistent \nwith international human rights obligations and to communicate these on a voluntary basis to \nWHO; \n(11) to develop, as appropriate, and in coordination with existing and emerging regional hubs \nand support mechanisms, effective partnerships with stakeholders from across all sectors in the \nuse of digital health; \n2. \nREQUESTS the Director-General: \n(1) \nto develop, within e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the requests to Member States, including data protection legislation and partnerships across sectors. It then lists requests to the Director-General, starting with developing a global strategy on digital health and including guidance, a repository of evidence and collaboration with other UN bodies.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
